 ## Known limitations (as of this review)
 
 1. **The live OpenAI API call has not yet been confirmed with a real key in this conversation.** Every test and every sandbox check so far has used a stub client. This capstone's own convention (per M2–M4) is not to consider a milestone fully done until a real call has actually succeeded.
-2. **`backend/prisma/migrations/` is not included in this archive** — never generated in this build environment (Prisma's CLI can't reach `binaries.prisma.sh` here). See "Verification status" above for exactly what that means for Feature 4 specifically. The real migration history only exists on the machine where `prisma migrate dev` is actually run. Before committing, copy that local `backend/prisma/migrations/` folder into the repo — it is not covered by `.gitignore` and should be committed alongside the schema.
+2. **Migrations:** `backend/prisma/migrations/` (5 migrations through `add_report`) IS present in the GitHub snapshot audited on 2026-10-23; the earlier note saying it was missing was stale. Applying them to a real database is still unverified in the audit environment (no Postgres / Prisma engine download available) — run `npx prisma migrate deploy` against a scratch database and confirm.
+3. **New AI safeguards (see below) are verified only with stub clients.** No real OpenAI call, real Postgres run, or real Chromium render was performed for them.
+
+## AI safeguards (deterministic, tested with stubs)
+
+- `src/grounding.js` — after the model rewrites CV bullets, every bullet is compared with the user's original at the same index. A bullet that introduces a **new number/metric** or a **new tool/technology/proper-noun term** is **reverted to the original** and reported (`grounding[]` in the `/tailor` response; `inJobDescription: true` marks likely keyword-stuffing). Lexical only: it will not catch semantic inflation ("contributed" → "led") — the user must still review the output.
+- `src/llm.js` — output count must equal input count (previously only requested in the prompt); request `timeout`/`maxRetries` set via `REQUEST_OPTIONS`.
+- `src/promptSafety.js` — job descriptions and bullets are fenced as untrusted data and delimiter-forging tags are stripped. A mitigation, not a guarantee.
+- `src/jobAnalysis.js` (not yet routed) — structured job-description extraction. Items the model labels `stated` must carry a quote found verbatim in the posting, otherwise they are relabeled `inferred`; keywords not literally in the posting are dropped.
+- `src/fit.js` (not yet routed) — requirement-vs-evidence matching with `supported | partial | missing | unclear`. No numeric score is produced; with no CV evidence everything is `unclear`, never `missing`.
+
+## Tests (updated)
+
+`npm test` runs everything. Pure suites (`validation`, `auth`, `llm`, `grounding`, `jobAnalysis`, `fit`) need no database. DB-backed suites (`applications`, `report` runtime tests) now require `TEST_DATABASE_URL` pointing at a **dedicated disposable database** and are skipped when it is unset — they no longer fall back to the dev database or a committed password.
